# fleet_round_open_witness.rish -- the round-open tells its states apart, and clears a rebase first.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/f/fleet_round_open_witness.rish
#
# `tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh` runs `git reset --hard xy/main` at every round-open, roughly every
# twenty minutes, on each of the eight live seats in `construction/fleet-roster.kyri`. It ran that
# way with no control at all until REDS %428. Destructive authority on that many trees earns a
# standing guard.
#
# The fault that earned this witness: the script modeled no interrupted rebase, and all three of
# its later steps misread one -- the conflicted worktree reads dirty and gets stashed, HEAD is
# detached at a half-replayed commit and gets classified, and the reset abandons the rebase and
# leaves the real branch behind. Against the elder script the control fails 5 of its 14 legs, and
# the elder prints `already on the anointed order` over a standing corpse.
#
# THE SECOND FAULT, REDS %503: this witness guarded six states and planted five. Seventeen legs
# proved behind, level, dirty, mid-rebase, an unreachable remote, and the dead-letter box. The
# `else` that runs `git branch`, `git push xy` and `reset --hard` together stood outside all of
# them. Behind it one classifier answered for three states. Ten commits parked between 20260828
# and 20260906 stayed on their branches while main moved on. The script now attempts the
# re-derivation its own header already prescribes, and reaches for the park only where git refuses.
# So the park keeps every case it was right about, and hands back the laps it was taking. The
# whole account rests at `construction/archive/REDS-the-test-that-cannot-fail-rows-499-503.md`,
# and the legs that plant those three states are A, B and C of
# `tools/fixtures/f/fleet_round_open_control.sh`.

say "fleet-round-open: Language EN -- each tree state told apart by name, and a rebase cleared before anything reads it."
say "fleet-round-open: Style Gauge, Meter -- every leg run on real repositories in a throwaway pen, never described."
say "fleet-round-open: Lens TAME -- safety first: this script's one verb is `reset --hard`, on trees that are not its own."

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the script and its control both live.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the script under test must stand before any reading of it is believed.
let present = run ["test" "-f" "tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh"]
assert present.ok else "tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh is missing -- the fleet has no round-open"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/f/fleet_round_open_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "fleet-round-open: a planted case read wrong -- see the control's own lines"
assert control.out contains "fail=0" else "fleet-round-open: the control closed with a failing leg"

# invariant: the rebase clause is in the script rather than only in the control's expectations.
let clause = run ["grep" "-q" "rebase --abort" "tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh"]
assert clause.ok else "fleet-round-open: the script no longer clears an interrupted rebase"

# invariant: the diverged branch attempts the re-derivation before it reaches for the park, so a
# lost race lands as a lost race (REDS %503). Read from the script itself rather than inferred from
# the control, since a control stays green on a shape the script has since let go.
let rederive = run ["grep" "-q" "git rebase xy/main" "tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh"]
assert rederive.ok else "fleet-round-open: the diverged branch no longer attempts the re-derivation"

# invariant: the control reaches that branch. A leg count reads weakly here; the state's own name
# in the control holds exactly while a leg plants it.
let planted = run ["grep" "-q" "ORDINARY LOST RACE" "tools/fixtures/f/fleet_round_open_control.sh"]
assert planted.ok else "fleet-round-open: no control leg plants the diverged state"

say "fleet-round-open: GREEN -- behind, level, ahead, dirty, mid-rebase, and all three divergences each answered by name."
